## Role

Members, onDuty, permission strings. TWO HONEST LIMITS, stated: `onDuty` is hand-set (no platform scheduler — rotation is a human act), and `permissions` is DATA for the consumer, not an ACL (realm permissions are the enforcement layer). A workflow `requires-role` guard compares the transition's role name with the role names the caller passes to Run Workflow; it does not read this card.

```ts
import { Role } from '@cardstack/catalog/cards/service-desk/role';

@field role = linksTo(() => Role);
```

### Why a separate ladder

The service desk's Queue and Support Agent tiers route a Ticket; Role and Escalation model who is on duty to receive a case escalation and the acknowledgement clock on it. Escalate Ticket moves a ticket between tiers; Escalate Case records the climb.

### Non-goals

No duty rotation schedule; no identity — cards have no current-user concept, so actors are passed explicitly.
